# SPA routing + deploy-race protection.
#
# Rule 1 is the critical one: during a deploy there is a window where the new
# HTML references a hashed asset that has not propagated yet. Without this
# rule Pages serves index.html (200) for the missing asset URL, and the
# custom-domain cache rule for /assets/* caches that HTML under the JS URL
# for hours -> blank page. Returning a 404 instead makes the module load fail
# cleanly (the inline self-heal script in index.html then reloads once).
/assets/*    /404.html    404
/*           /index.html  200
